1. Implement parameterized queries/prepared statements for ALL database operations
2. Add input validation and sanitization
3. Implement rate limiting on login endpoint
4. Remove detailed error messages; use generic responses
5. Add CSRF tokens to login form
6. Enforce POST-only on login endpoint

**Short Term (Do Soon):**
7. Add security headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, etc.)
8. Implement account lockout after failed attempts
9. Add logging for all authentication attempts
10. Use password hashing (bcrypt/Argon2)
11. Implement proper session management with secure cookies (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)

**Medium Term (Do Before Production):**
12. Enable HTTPS/TLS with proper certificates
13. Implement Web Application Firewall (WAF)
14. Add security testing to CI/CD pipeline
15. Conduct regular security audits
16. Implement proper authorization checks (role-based access control)

